Upstream attribution (from the Musubi Tuner README):
- MiniMax-H3 transformer, video VAE, packing, text presentation and scheduler
  are adapted from Diffusers PR #14355 (Copyright The MiniMax Team and
  The HuggingFace Team, Apache-2.0).
- wan/ is modified from Wan2.1 (Apache-2.0).
- modules/convrot_int8_kernels.py is modified from comfy-kitchen (Apache-2.0).
- Other Musubi Tuner code is Apache-2.0; some is copied and modified from Diffusers.

Modifications made for Ultra AI Generator:
- Only the modules needed for MiniMax-H3 inference are included; training,
  dataset caching, other model architectures and the generation CLI are not.
- The package is renamed from `musubi_tuner` to `h3core` (imports rewritten)
  so it cannot collide with an installed musubi-tuner.
- minimax_h3/media.py: removed the unused import of the dataset
  ContentDatasource and turned its one type annotation (in a training-only
  helper) into a plain string.
- networks/lora_minimax_h3.py: LoRA target modules include "RefinerBlock"
  besides "DiTBlock", so LoRAs that adapt the text-token refiner (such as the
  H3 turbo LoRA) load completely. Training defaults are unaffected because the
  default target pattern only matches the main DiT blocks.
- minimax_h3/model.py: for sequences longer than 16384 tokens (TOKEN_CHUNK),
  the token-wise parts run in token chunks: the MLP, and in attention the qkv
  projection, q/k RMSNorm, RoPE and the output projection (written into
  full-length q/k/v buffers; the attention itself still sees the whole
  sequence). This changes only peak memory. Shorter sequences take the
  original code path unchanged.
